{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774710,"nonce":"a/fWdy3Pt7Ot/nF9DOU+pUzPto0=","title":"feat(web-ui): engineer dashboard — action inbox, activity feed, all-clear","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #10 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `feat/web-ui-dashboard-action-inbox` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-15T11:18:32Z · Merged: 2026-07-15T11:37:32Z\n\n\nReframes the web-ui landing tier (`/`) from a **repo directory** into a **first-person engineer dashboard** keyed on the signed-in actor. The page now answers the engineer's actual daily loop — *is anything blocked on me? what's my stuff doing? take me to my repo* — instead of just listing repositories.\n\nThree stacked modules:\n\n1. **Waiting on you** — an *action inbox* of runs frozen until you decide:\n   - `approve` (deploy gate), `input` (manual gate), `re-run` (failed run), `resume` (held run)\n   - The verb chip carries each row; button weight follows the verb (Approve = pine primary, Re-run/Resume = ghost).\n2. **Your activity** — your recent runs across all repos, in-flight pinned first. Inbox runs are suppressed here, so a run shows once: **act** (inbox) vs **observe** (feed), never both.\n3. **Your repos** — the existing repo grid, now the navigation floor.\n\nWhen the inbox and in-flight list are both empty, the page collapses to a deliberate **\"All clear — nothing needs you\"** banner + repo grid — never an idle/blank surface.\n\n\n- **Operator/fleet metrics deliberately omitted** (success rate, throughput, queue depth) — those belong in Grafana/observability. This surface is the *individual engineer's* loop.\n- **Honesty:** only `re-run` maps to a wired action today (`RunDetail` restart). `approve`/`input`/`resume` need the ADR-0037 gate backend and are tagged `representative` on-screen. Data is driven by the existing representative `catalog.ts` (`actionInbox()`, `myActivity()`), same pattern as the rest of the repo-first surfaces.\n- The `active / all clear` **pill is a prototype-only control** to preview both layouts; it's removed once data is real.\n\n\nWire **Your activity** to the real `listRuns` filtered by actor, so half the page runs on live data while the gate rows stay representative until ADR-0037 lands.\n\n\n- `tsc --noEmit` clean.\n- Rendered both states in the browser (active + all-clear), light theme.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}